@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# HORIZON lever diagnostic protocol — 2026-09-10
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. This file is fixed before either horizon arm is fit.
+
+## Question and fixed inputs
+
+- Diagnose whether C3 convergence under-run is addressed by more full-batch
+  updates (Arm A) or by minibatch updates (Arm B). This is one route and one
+  seed, not a learning-rate grid and not a learning-rate selection.
+- Use the twelve fixed C3 LOAO anchors named by the LRSWEEP harness, including
+  only size>=2 rows for training and retaining the declared hard-zero
+  empty/singleton predictions for held-out diagnostics.
+- Use model seed `V025_LEARNER/seed/1` (`6407676579069309528`), C3 learning
+  rate `1e-3`, and every other architecture and Adam literal unchanged.
+- Import and reuse the LRSWEEP harness at
+  `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/lr-convergence-sweep/run_sweep.py`
+  (SHA-256 `dde9a8e93a54d67dbe601a47465e47108fb27f57e5b7d9213cf3a8a1a0300fc6`),
+  its frozen rule (SHA-256
+  `0484ffbf3ea2447e0bb0067a8067739c069c1550d48dc0629b9fbf3af20f9b19`),
+  and its results (SHA-256
+  `9424c6d8c00906e5b86f9ed9d00e4c8b2e8a8bd3a598f3f61677c6eafaf84861`)
+  directly and without modifying those artifacts.
+
+## Common cadence and rule
+
+- Cap both arms at 4,000 optimizer updates and evaluate at update 0 and every
+  100 updates through 4,000.
+- At each destination cadence `k`, apply LRSWEEP's identical four checks to
+  `k-100 -> k`: objective relative absolute motion <= 0.01; held-out level R2
+  absolute motion <= 0.01; held-out within-group ordering absolute motion <=
+  0.005; held-out top-1 absolute motion <= 0.005. The first finite destination
+  cadence satisfying all four is that arm's first admissible update.
+- The checkpoint training objective is always evaluated on the complete LOAO
+  training fold, including for Arm B. A last-minibatch loss is not used.
+
+## Arms
+
+- Arm A: the LRSWEEP C3 full-batch gradient aggregation verbatim, one Adam
+  update over all eleven training anchors per optimizer step.
+- Arm B: batch size 256. For each LOAO fold, concatenate the eleven training
+  anchors in the fixed LRSWEEP filename order. Initialise an independent PCG64
+  generator from the SHA-256 domain seed
+  `V025_HORIZON/C3/minibatch-shuffle/seed/1`. At the start of every pass,
+  generate a permutation of all training rows; consume consecutive batches of
+  256 without replacement within that pass; include the final remainder batch;
+  then reshuffle for the next pass. Rows recur across passes. Each fold starts
+  a fresh generator at the same declared shuffle seed. This deterministic
+  ordering is separate from the unchanged model-initialisation seed.
+- Minibatching is a training-procedure change, not a hyperparameter.
+
+## Scope and resources
+
+- Metrics are convergence diagnostics only and are never evidence about EE.
+  Compute no EE quantity and perform no selection on EE.
+- Read only the twelve C3 files fixed in LRSWEEP. Do not discover or read any
+  evaluation-only claim dates.
+- Run both arms sequentially in one Python process using only
+  `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`, niceness 19, all named BLAS
+  thread variables equal to one, and an address-space limit below 3 GiB.
+- Print progress as `step k/N` and print peak RSS. If one-minute load average
+  exceeds 30 at a cadence boundary, stop before more training and record a
+  load pause rather than pushing through.
+

diff --git a/.scratch/horizon-lever/run_horizon.py b/.scratch/horizon-lever/run_horizon.py
